  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 200°C. Warm the olive oil in a large ovenproof casserole over medium heat, then brown the sausages on all sides for 5–7 minutes. Remove and set aside.",
    "Add the onion and carrot to the casserole and cook for 6–8 minutes until softened and lightly golden. Stir in the garlic, thyme, oregano and paprika and cook for 1 minute more.",
    "Add the canned tomatoes, cannellini beans, water, bay leaves, salt and black pepper. Stir well and bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Nestle the sausages back into the bean mixture. Cover and bake for 35 minutes until the sauce is bubbling and the sausages are cooked through.",
    "Mix the breadcrumbs with the parmesan and sprinkle over the top. Return to the oven uncovered for 10–12 minutes until the topping is crisp and golden.",
    "Scatter with chopped parsley and serve hot, making sure each portion gets plenty of beans, sauce and sausage."
